@baseUrl = https://localhost:7146
@apiUrl = {{baseUrl}}/api/v1

# Fill in after logging in via the "Login" request below (POST {{apiUrl}}/users/auth).
@token = REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN
@userId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# See the "API responses — Result Pattern" section in the repo README for the full
# explanation of what each response shape below means and why.

### =====================================================================
### SUCCESS — 200 OK with a value (ResultT<T>.Success)
### =====================================================================

# Paginated read — always 200 OK + PagedResult<SkillDto> on success.
GET {{apiUrl}}/ability/pagination?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10
Accept: application/json

# Expected 200 body — the body IS the PagedResult<T>, not a raw list, and not wrapped in
# { isSuccess, value }. totalPages is computed server-side, not left for the client to derive:
# {
#   "items": [
#     { "skillId": "3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6", "name": "Advanced C#", "registeredAt": "2026-09-12T14:30:00Z" }
#   ],
#   "totalItems": 1,
#   "currentPage": 1,
#   "totalPages": 1
# }

###

# Login — 200 OK + TokenResponseDto { accessToken, refreshToken }. Copy accessToken into @token above.
POST {{apiUrl}}/users/auth
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "someone@example.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### =====================================================================
### SUCCESS — Create*CommandHandler (also 200 OK, not 201 — see README)
### =====================================================================

# Every Create*CommandHandler returns ResultT<T>.Success(dto), so this is 200 OK + SkillDto,
# same status as any other read/update. Requires a valid Bearer token.
POST {{apiUrl}}/ability
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Advanced C#",
  "userId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

# Expected 200 body — the body IS the SkillDto, no envelope around it:
# {
#   "skillId": "3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6",
#   "name": "Advanced C#",
#   "registeredAt": "2026-09-12T14:30:00Z"
# }

### =====================================================================
### ERROR — 404 Not Found (Error.NotFound -> ResultFilter -> ProblemDetails)
### =====================================================================

# UserId that doesn't exist -> CreateSkillCommandHandler returns Error.NotFound.
POST {{apiUrl}}/ability
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Any name",
  "userId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111"
}

# Expected 404 body:
# {
#   "type": "https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc9110#section-15.5.5",
#   "title": "Not Found",
#   "status": 404,
#   "detail": "The specified user was not found.",
#   "errorCode": "404"
# }

### =====================================================================
### ERROR — 409 Conflict (Error.Conflict) — duplicate resource
### =====================================================================

# Same request as above but with a "name" that already exists for some skill ->
# CreateSkillCommandHandler returns Error.Conflict instead of creating a duplicate.
POST {{apiUrl}}/ability
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Advanced C#",
  "userId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

### =====================================================================
### ERROR — 400 Validation, flavor 1: FluentValidation (before the handler runs)
### =====================================================================

# Empty "name" fails CreateSkillValidator in the MediatR pipeline, before CreateSkillCommandHandler
# ever runs. Caught by ExceptionHandlingMiddleware, NOT by ResultFilter -> different body shape
# (see "Three response shapes still coexist" in the README).
POST {{apiUrl}}/ability
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "",
  "userId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

# Expected 400 body (note "errors", not "errorCode"):
# {
#   "type": "ValidationFailure",
#   "title": "Validation errors",
#   "status": 400,
#   "errors": { "Name": ["The skill name is required."] }
# }

### =====================================================================
### ERROR — 400 Validation, flavor 2: business rule (Error.Validation -> ResultFilter)
### =====================================================================

# Incomplete profile (no skills/interests, or missing Expert/Recruiter role) is a business-state
# check that FluentValidation can't express (it needs a DB lookup) -> reaches the handler, which
# returns Error.Validation. Same ProblemDetails shape as the 404 example above (errorCode, not errors).
GET {{apiUrl}}/users/{{userId}}/recommendations?pageNumber=1&pageSize=10
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### =====================================================================
### ERROR — 403 Forbidden (Error.Forbidden) — no [Authorize] needed to trigger this one
### =====================================================================

# Confirming an account with a code that exists but belongs to a different user.
# ConfirmAccountAsync (CodeService.ConfirmAccountAsync) exercises FIVE different error types
# depending on the input, all on this one endpoint:
#   - userId doesn't exist            -> 404 Error.NotFound
#   - code doesn't exist              -> 404 Error.NotFound
#   - code belongs to another user    -> 403 Error.Forbidden   (this example)
#   - code isn't an account-confirm code -> 403 Error.Forbidden
#   - code was already used           -> 409 Error.Conflict
#   - code expired/invalid            -> 400 Error.Validation
#   - all good                        -> 204 No Content (Result.Success(), no value)
POST {{apiUrl}}/users/confirm-account?userId=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000&code=someone-elses-code

### =====================================================================
### ERROR — 401 Unauthorized — missing/invalid token on an [Authorize] endpoint
### =====================================================================

# No Authorization header at all. IMPORTANT: this does NOT go through ResultFilter/ProblemDetails —
# JwtBearerEvents.OnChallenge (Trivo.Infrastructure.Shared/DependencyInjection.cs) writes the body
# directly with Newtonsoft.Json, so the shape and casing differ from every other error above.
POST {{apiUrl}}/ability
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Advanced C#",
  "userId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
}

# Expected 401 body (PascalCase — Newtonsoft default, not the System.Text.Json camelCase used elsewhere):
# { "HasError": true, "Error": "An unexpected authentication error occurred" }

### =====================================================================
### SUCCESS — 204 No Content (Result.Success(), no value)
### =====================================================================

# No controller in this API returns a bare Result today (they all return ResultT<T>), so there's no
# live endpoint to call here yet. The example above (confirm-account, happy path) is the closest one:
# ConfirmAccountAsync's underlying Result IS a bare Result, so a correct confirm-account call returns
# 204 No Content with an empty body, once you have a real, unused, non-expired confirmation code:
POST {{apiUrl}}/users/confirm-account?userId=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000&code=REPLACE_WITH_REAL_CODE
